  "final_answer_preview": "According to the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, a person who commits an act while being of unsound mind is not considered to have committed an offence if they are incapable of knowing the nature of the act or that it is wrong (Section 22 Body, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023). Additionally, if an act is done in good faith for the benefit of a person of unsound mind, it is not an offence due to any harm it may cause (Section 27 Body, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023). However, this does not apply if the act involves the voluntary causing of grievous hurt unless it is for specific purposes such as preventing death or curing a grievous disease (Section 27(c), Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023).",
